# Skill: Orchestration Hardening

Purpose:
  Engineering skill for making multi-agent orchestration reliable — the
  patterns behind SDDRA's chain graph, checkpoints, interrupts, and loop
  protection. Use when designing agent teams, failure handling, or
  resume-from-crash behavior.

Owns: engineering/orchestration-hardening.sdd

Source: research round 3 r3 (2026-09-07) — LangGraph, Temporal, UMAF,
  Cognition map-reduce-and-manage, Microsoft Agent Framework; sources
  cited in .sdd/runtime/state.sdd + contract.sdd Phase 149 additions.

Patterns:
  topology_selection:
    - "can one coordinator hold the full plan?" -> supervisor (SDDRA
      hub-and-spoke IS this — validated)
    - map-reduce-and-manage: manager splits, children read-only, manager
      synthesizes (single-threaded writes — Cognition)
    - unstructured swarms: anti-pattern (quadratic chatter, loops)
  durable_checkpoints:
    - per-arm-boundary snapshots keyed by run ID; resume never re-executes
    - boundary discipline only (>75% of turns have no recovery state)
  structural_interrupts:
    - hard interrupt before irreversible actions (LLM cannot bypass)
    - state persisted pre-interrupt; resume with decision object
    - approval timeout -> auto-reject for irreversible
  tiered_loop_caps:
    - chain 50 / arm 10 / agent 5-8; error-spiral detector (3
      consecutive failures -> wrap-up); ALWAYS-FORWARD
  failure_stack:
    - retry+backoff(3) -> fallback chain -> circuit breaker per arm
      (3 failures/10 min -> OPEN 15 min -> HALF_OPEN probe)
  typed_outcomes:
    - SUCCESS/PARTIAL/BLOCKED/NEEDS_CLARIFICATION/POLICY_VIOLATION/
      TOOL_ERROR/UNSAFE before escalation — NL apologies are not signal
  observability:
    - OTel: 1 trace per run, 1 span per arm; GenAI semantic conventions
  deterministic_routing:
    - LLM proposes, code disposes (governance kernel) — SDDRA
      workflow.yaml rules already are this

AntiPatterns:
  - peer-to-peer swarms between arms; 3+ supervisor levels; blanket
    per-message checkpointing; blanket max_iter=50 everywhere

Rules:
  [OH1] Apply via .sdd/runtime/state.sdd + contract.sdd +
       LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd — specs are authority.
  [OH2] Orchestration designs cite pattern provenance.

